        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "Thanks for taking a look. The first version of this PR printed the resolved path at the end of the same line that exists today:\r\n```diff\r\n- Using data directory /home/larry/.bitcoin\r\n+ Using data directory /home/larry/.bitcoin (/sd/.bitcoin)\r\n```\r\nAnd it added that path only if it was different from the \"Using\" path. But after more thought, it seems better to log a new line (\"Resolved\") and leave the existing log line unchanged (in case scripts exist somewhere that expect the current format). I also thought it would be better to always log this new Resolved line so future scripts can look for it without needing logic to fall back to \"Using\" if \"Resolved\" doesn't exist. So I force-pushed those changes. But I forgot to update the title; fixed now.\r\n\r\nSounds like you would like the Resolved line to only print if it's different; I can make that change, I don't feel strongly either way.\r\n\r\nNo, I'm not thinking this is part of a broader effort to improve symlink support. AFAIK symlinks are already fully supported. It's just a self-contained PR that would have helped me personally, since I saved a bunch of `debug.log` files and later wasn't sure whether each corresponded to an SSD or an HDD data directory run (because I had changed a symlink). Plus, it seems generally useful to know where the actual data directory is.\r\n\r\nI can make the logging of that Resolved line conditional so it doesn't print the same path as the Using line, maybe I'll wait for a few more opinions.",
